  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 1048 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nThe work week will be largely influenced by upper level ridging \nand subsequent sfc high pressure to our west, slowly shifting into\nthe lower Mississippi Valley. In turn, heat will build into the \nregion through the early week with highs rising into the mid to \nupper 90s along with heat index temperatures in the 100-109 degree\nrange. Heat products will likely be considered in future updates \nthis weekend, with the highest chance of one being issued landing \non Tuesday. Mid week, slight relief from the heat is expected as a\ncold front pushes south through the area along with increased \ncloud cover. However, temperatures will likely still be in the \nupper 80s to lower 90s. Confidence is low on how far south this \nfrontal boundary will travel as it is dependent on the track and \ndepth of an upper level trough and coexisting sfc low digging into\nthe Appalachian region. Rain chances mid week have been kept with\nblended guidance- remaining low (20% or less).",
